{
  "id": "corridor-illusion",
  "term": "corridor illusion",
  "definition": "The corridor illusion is a visual size illusion in which two physically identical circles look different in size when one is shown at the near end of a corridor and the other at the far end. The circle placed farther away appears larger, reflecting a mismatch between perceived and actual size created by pictorial depth cues.",
